# Every text file is checked out as the repository holds it, LF, on every
# platform (lane fix-windows-crlf): the tests read the documents, the
# workflows and the sources as text and compare them by line and by sentence
# with LF text, and a Windows runner's checkout (core.autocrlf=true) handed
# them CRLF. Six tests of tests/arch_ci_runs_every_test.rs and
# tests/front_page.rs were red there alone on the full matrix of 2026-11-16.
# One rule for all text, not a list of the paths those six read: a list goes
# stale with the next test that reads a file (bsv-rs#367 mended such readers
# one at a time). The index holds no CRLF, so no file is renormalized. The
# lines below stay and override this one for their paths: no conversion at all.
* text=auto eol=lf
# The shared vectors and the recorded fixtures are read byte for byte (their
# sha256 is pinned in the tests that load them; a vector is never edited to
# make a test pass). No line-ending conversion on any checkout: #146's whole-
# suite run on Windows found hkdf_wycheproof red on CRLF bytes alone.
tests/vectors/** -text
tests/fixtures/** -text
fuzz/corpus/** -text
# The BIP-39 wordlists are parsed at compile time, one word per LF-terminated
# line; a CRLF checkout would put a CR in every word (the parser refuses it)
# and move each file's pinned sha256 (#89).
src/compat/bip39/wordlists/*.txt -text
# The certificate collation table is parsed at compile time, one DUCET row per
# LF-terminated line; a CRLF checkout puts a CR in every line and the parser
# refuses it (#249, the same rule as the wordlists).
src/wallet/collation_latin1.txt -text
# The recorded chain headers and the testnet header vector are read byte for
# byte (80-byte headers end to end; tests/data/chain_headers/README.md gives
# each file's source). Until this line only git's NUL heuristic kept the four
# .bin files from conversion: a file of pinned bytes that held no NUL in its
# leading 8000 bytes would have been converted as text (the strength read of
# pull request #1021, row (b); lane after-tag-hygiene). The other files under
# the two paths are held with LF in the index and are checked out as held.
tests/data/** -text
tests/chain_vectors/** -text
